{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0EZW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-Rf-star-colim}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-f-star-general}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{varieties-lemma-separably-closed-field-connected-components}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:03bcd7b8ab0489f0d6e042229a6869a6f398dd7b7964e0c176215d45784eab88", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:30e54ef383424651db387617bbfc74099ccf7580cf458b2fdb8d9138ea27e9e1", "source_text": "We may work locally on <MATH_0001>. Hence we may assume <MATH_0002> is affine.\nThen we can write <MATH_0003> as a cofiltered limit of affine schemes of\nfinite type over <MATH_0004>. By Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe may assume that <MATH_0005> is of finite type over <MATH_0006>.\nThen Lemma <REF_0002>\napplies because any scheme of finite\ntype over a separably closed field is a finite disjoint\nunion of connected and geometrically connected schemes\n(see Varieties, Lemma\n<REF_0003>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7391531e18d5ce1823697e94a712481579bec592af7e27888f10370bce2c2b5b", "unit_id": "tag:0EZY:proof"}
